@startuml
title SIC/XE parseLine - Detailed Horizontal Parser Flow
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #455A64
  ArrowColor #546E7A
}

[*] --> Normalize

state "1. Normalize and filter line\n\n- Remove trailing CR/LF\n- If column 1 is '.', ignore the line\n- Strip ';' comment outside apostrophe quotes\n- Return null for blank/comment-only input" as Normalize

state "2. Read first field\n\nnextField skips isSpace and scans\nto the next whitespace boundary" as FirstField

state "3. Decide label or operation\n\nLookup uses operationMnemonic + uppercase\n(ignores leading '+' and suffix after ',')\n\nKnown opcode/directive -> operation\nOtherwise -> label; validate identifier and\nreject register names as labels\n\nRead next field as operation; if absent,\nreturn label-only Statement" as Classify

state "4. Parse operation modifiers\n\nRecord 1-based mnemonic column\nLeading '+' sets extended\nSuffix accepts case-insensitive ',p' or ',b'\nStore selector; remove it from mnemonic\nUppercase mnemonic; resolve directive first,\nthen instruction; unknown name reports error\n'+' on a directive reports error" as Resolve

state "5. Split operands and apply alias\n\nCapture remaining text; trim trailing whitespace\nRecord 1-based operand column\nsplitOperands splits commas outside quotes,\ntrims each field, and preserves its start column\n\nFor non-extended instructions, a register-like\nfirst field may select ADDR/SUBR/MULR/DIVR/\nCOMPR or TIXR alias" as Split

state "6A. Instruction schema dispatch\n\nNone: require 0 fields\nMemory: require 1-2; parse # / @ / simple\naddress expression; optional second field\nrequires '$X'; reject indexing with # or @\nReg: 1 register\nRegReg: 2 registers\nRegCount: register + expression\nNumber: 1 expression\n\nRegister parser requires '$' and resolves\nname through registerNumber" as InstructionPath

state "6B. Directive dispatch\n\nNOBASE: 0 fields\nEND / ORG: 0-1 expression\nSTART / RESB / RESW / BASE / EQU: 1 expression\nBYTE / WORD: at least 1 item\n\nC'...' literal -> one byte per source char\nX'...' literal -> even-length hex, decode pairs\nWORD rejects literals; non-literals use\nparseExpression and become DataItems" as DirectivePath

state "Expression service boundary\n\nparseExprField passes text, source line,\nand starting column to parseExpression\nExpression parsing/evaluation is a separate\nservice from this line parser" as ExpressionBoundary

state "Validation and diagnostics\n\narity() checks operand counts\nfail() reports line + 1-based column\nand sets Statement.valid = false\nLiteral errors cover malformed form,\nodd hex length, and invalid hex digits\nParsing can continue after recoverable errors" as Errors

state "Return Statement\n\nSyntax, source text/positions, parsed\noperands and validity are populated\nAddress, size, and emitted bytes are\nfilled later by assembler passes" as Result

Normalize --> FirstField
FirstField --> Classify
Classify --> Resolve : operation found
Classify --> Result : blank / comment / label-only
Resolve --> Split : known instruction or directive
Resolve --> Result : unknown operation
Split --> InstructionPath : instruction
Split --> DirectivePath : directive
InstructionPath --> ExpressionBoundary : expression field(s)
DirectivePath --> ExpressionBoundary : expression item(s)
InstructionPath --> Errors
DirectivePath --> Errors
ExpressionBoundary --> Errors
Errors --> Result
Result --> [*]

note top of Normalize
There is no standalone Lexer object or general token stream.
Lexical work happens in parser.cpp helper functions.
end note

note bottom of Resolve
The parser checks selectors against the memory operand schema.
The assembler engine later enforces format-3 restrictions.
end note
@enduml
